After the search integration returned HTTP 402, direct DuckDuckGo HTML search worked and supplied community leads. Their contents are treated only as leads/qualified historical reports, not independently verified benchmark evidence; one discussion explicitly displays AI-assisted authorship. The official TokenRhythm homepage, model page and API docs were independently fetched, and the authenticated native catalog failure was confirmed via shell. Fresh public gateway/artifact queries were empty. This is a bounded no-evidence/access-limited conclusion, not a global web outage or proof of model nonexistence. No peer findings, local metadata or other model numbers were used.

